21	1_2	1	2	2	1	Our road trip March 2026:\nThe station wagon was packed to the brim, a Tetris masterpiece of suitcases and coolers. As the engine hummed to life, the familiar scent of old upholstery and sunscreen signaled the official start of the summer road trip.\n\nThe highway stretched out like a ribbon of possibilities. Inside, the atmosphere was electric. Instead of staring at screens, the family engaged in a spirited game of "I Spy," finding joy in the mundane—a rusted silo, a stray cow, or a license plate from a distant state. Laughter rippled through the car when the youngest member insisted a cloud looked exactly like a giant slice of pizza.\n\nBy midday, they pulled over at a hidden scenic overlook. They sat on the tailgate, sharing sandwiches and watching the wind dance through the valley below. No one checked their watches; the only schedule was the movement of the sun.\n\nAs evening approached, the sky bled into hues of violet and gold. The kids eventually drifted off to sleep against the windows, exhausted from a day of discovery. Up front, the parents shared a quiet smile, fueled by caffeine and the simple, profound peace of being exactly where they needed to be: together, moving forward.	{"to": 1, "from": 2, "text": "Our road trip March 2026:\\nThe station wagon was packed to the brim, a Tetris masterpiece of suitcases and coolers. As the engine hummed to life, the familiar scent of old upholstery and sunscreen signaled the official start of the summer road trip.\\n\\nThe highway stretched out like a ribbon of possibilities. Inside, the atmosphere was electric. Instead of staring at screens, the family engaged in a spirited game of \\"I Spy,\\" finding joy in the mundane—a rusted silo, a stray cow, or a license plate from a distant state. Laughter rippled through the car when the youngest member insisted a cloud looked exactly like a giant slice of pizza.\\n\\nBy midday, they pulled over at a hidden scenic overlook. They sat on the tailgate, sharing sandwiches and watching the wind dance through the valley below. No one checked their watches; the only schedule was the movement of the sun.\\n\\nAs evening approached, the sky bled into hues of violet and gold. The kids eventually drifted off to sleep against the windows, exhausted from a day of discovery. Up front, the parents shared a quiet smile, fueled by caffeine and the simple, profound peace of being exactly where they needed to be: together, moving forward."}	2026-05-22 22:19:17.161946-04
